<Layout
	title="About Bezerk"
	description="A magnetic, paintable rain frog sculpture who lives for hide-and-seek in happy little places."
	pubDate={new Date('Mar 01 2026')}
	heroImage="/images/bezerk-at-home.jpg"
>
	<p>
		Bezerk is a palm-sized tribute to the African rain frog: round, warty, and deeply committed to
		sitting somewhere that makes you smile. He is not a toy you throw across the room. He is a
		traveling guest who sticks to metal and expects reasonable hospitality.
	</p>

	<p>
		<strong>Magnets in the feet</strong> mean he can hug table legs, shelves, and any ferrous surface
		that will have him. <strong>Paintable plastic</strong> means every home can give him a new look—or
		leave him blank like a little moon rock with attitude.
	</p>

	<p>
		The tradition: hide bezerk in a cheerful spot. Someone discovers him, takes him along, maybe
		adds a paint pass, then hides him again for the next person. No scoreboard. Just small surprises
		looping through friends and family.
	</p>

	<p>
		This site is the field journal—hides, color experiments, and wherever he turns up next. If you
		have a bezerk story, you are already part of the lore.
	</p>
</Layout>
